            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59869",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "js-yaml: js-yaml: Denial of Service via crafted YAML documents"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "js-yaml is a JavaScript YAML parser and dumper. From 3.0.0 before 3.15.0 and from 4.0.0 before 4.3.0, js-yaml can spend quadratic CPU time parsing a document whose size grows only linearly when a chain of mappings uses merge keys where each mapping merges the previous one. This issue is fixed in versions 3.15.0 and 4.3.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59869",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-59869\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: js-yaml\nFixed Version: 3.15.0, 4.3.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-59869](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59869)\njs-yaml is a JavaScript YAML parser and dumper. From 3.0.0 before 3.15.0 and from 4.0.0 before 4.3.0, js-yaml can spend quadratic CPU time parsing a document whose size grows only linearly when a chain of mappings uses merge keys where each mapping merges the previous one. This issue is fixed in versions 3.15.0 and 4.3.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-59869**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|js-yaml|3.15.0, 4.3.0|[CVE-2026-59869](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59869)|\n\njs-yaml is a JavaScript YAML parser and dumper. From 3.0.0 before 3.15.0 and from 4.0.0 before 4.3.0, js-yaml can spend quadratic CPU time parsing a document whose size grows only linearly when a chain of mappings uses merge keys where each mapping merges the previous one. This issue is fixed in versions 3.15.0 and 4.3.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
